* Symptom

Found while fixing errno-setvar-accepted-by-vendors (2026-11-04).
=autolisp-test/tests/sysvar/inventory-coverage.lsp= says it is GENERATED
by =autolisp-test/tools/generate-sysvar-corpus.lisp=, but regenerating it

#+begin_example
sbcl --non-interactive --load autolisp-test/tools/generate-sysvar-corpus.lisp --eval '(generate)'
#+end_example

changes far more than the entry being edited: ~120 lines go, among them
=sysvar-celtype-getvar-default=, =sysvar-cmaterial-getvar-default= and the
=sysvar-cmdline*-getvar-default= tests (BricsCAD "RGB: 50 54 56 (Settings
dialog) ..." defaults). Either the tracked file was edited by hand, or the
generator (or the inventory's :default fields) changed without the file
being regenerated.

For errno-setvar the generator was updated and the one ERRNO entry
patched by hand, to keep the change reviewable.

* To do

1. Find which side moved (git log of the generator, the inventory and the
   generated file) and decide which tests are right.
2. Regenerate, and add a check target (like check-dialect-warnings-annex)
   so the drift cannot come back silently.
